              "a11yRetry": "Retry the task. Reset all responses and start the task over again.",
              "textField": "We cannot use acetylcholine as a drug. It has a half life of one second in the body and it would act on all acetylcholine receptors in the muscles, the PNS and the brain. WAY too many problems to use acetylcholine. Instead, we use direct and indirect acting acetylcholine ‘agonists’.  Some direct acting ones, like *pilocarpine* are used only as eye drops are used to treat eye conditions like *glaucoma*. Another direct acting non-selective cholinergic agonist is *bethanechol* which is used to treat *non-obstructive urinary retention* like that which occurs after surgery. Some indirect acting ones like *neostigmine* are good for *myasthenia gravis*, while others like *donepezil* treat *Alzheimer’s disease*"
